The hydrogen atom mentioned in **(a)(i)** forms a covalent bond with one of the oxygen atoms of an $\text{NO}_2$ molecule. An $\text{NO}_2$ molecule has a single, unpaired electron on the nitrogen atom. All electrons are paired in an $\text{HNO}_2$ molecule.

Draw dot-and-cross diagrams of $\text{NO}_2$ and $\text{HNO}_2$ in the boxes. Show outer shell electrons only.

